fix: send contact email from the verified Resend domain (getassureai.com)

Resend rejects a from-address on a non-verified domain. assureproof.com is
not verified in Resend, so every /contact-submit submission since the
2026-11-15 R2->Workers cutover failed with 502 ("The assureproof.com domain
is not verified.") - a live probe on 2026-11-23 reproduced it.

- worker: SALES_INBOX -> sales@getassureai.com, EMAIL_FROM ->
  AssureProof Website <website@getassureai.com> (the verified domain the
  owner confirmed is integrated, receiving and sending).
- test_site_email_addresses_use_assureproof_com was enforcing the broken
  invariant; reshaped into test_worker_email_uses_the_verified_resend_domain:
  worker addresses must stay on the verified domain, and the legacy domain
  must still never leak onto built pages.
- docs/runbooks/ship-webpage.md: the original getassureai.com addresses
  were correct - the previous edit is reverted.
- docs/bot-policy-audit.md: email-delivery section with the incident
  record; the public-facing contact address (contact page, PoC error copy,
  security.txt Contact) remains [CONFIRM].

Local: pytest tests/ = 99 passed.
